.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt USB-WIFI-UPLINK.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm usb-wifi-uplink.sh
.Nd configure a USB Wi-Fi internet uplink
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar action Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm set
.Op Ar ssid Op Ar password Op Ar enabled
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
configures a spare USB Wi-Fi adapter as a routed client using stored
credentials, wpa_supplicant and systemd-networkd.
Run as root, including for status: a missing configuration is created
with defaults.
The default action is
.Cm reconcile .
.Pp
An eligible adapter has a wlan name outside wlan0 through wlan3,
uses USB, and is not assigned a mesh, HaLow or non-mesh radio role.
Morse and brcmfmac drivers are excluded.
The optional interface is preferred if eligible; otherwise an eligible
adapter is selected automatically.
.Pp
Actions are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm add , online , reconcile , connect
Write client configuration, restart the client service and request DHCP.
.It Cm remove , offline , disconnect
Stop the client and remove its generated Wi-Fi and network configuration.
.It Cm status-json , status
Print JSON describing adapter presence, association, address and service state.
.It Cm scan-json
Scan the eligible adapter and print nearby networks as JSON.
Restore an initially down adapter after success or failure.
Save the private scan list for five minutes for management-page selection.
.It Cm set-stdin
Read local management credentials as JSON from standard input.
Open and WPA2 Personal networks are supported.
A menu selection must match a selectable recent scan on the same adapter.
Save its BSSID to reconnect to the selected access point.
Passwords are never passed in process arguments by this action.
.It Cm set Op Ar ssid Op Ar password Op Ar enabled
Save credentials and attempt a connection.
Omitted or empty values default to SSID
.Li hotspot ,
password
.Li raspberry
and enabled value
.Li 1 .
Use
.Li 0
to stop an active uplink and disable future connection attempts.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/manet/usb-wifi-uplink.conf
Stored enabled flag, SSID, password, security and optional BSSID; mode 0600.
.It Pa /run/manet-usb-wifi-scan.json
Recent scan identity and network list; mode 0600.
.It Pa /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant-*-uplink.conf
Generated client credentials.
.It Pa /etc/systemd/network/20-*-usb-wifi-uplink.network
Generated DHCP client configuration.
.It Pa /etc/systemd/system/usb-wifi-client@.service
Client service template.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 when the action completes.
Connection actions return nonzero for a missing adapter, disabled uplink
or operating error; invalid arguments return 1.
The
.Cm set
action may save settings, print status JSON and return 0 even when
connection fails.
Use status output to check association and address assignment.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo usb-wifi-uplink.sh status
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ethernet-autodetect.sh 8
